==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|gussie up}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|*}} {{tlb|en|chiefly|US}}

# {{lb|en|informal|intransitive}} To [[don]] fancy clothing; to [[dress up]] particularly in flattering or specially altered garments.
#: {{syn|en|doll up}}
#: {{ux|en|You bet she'll '''gussy up''' for the party.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en-US|author=Ruth La Ferla|title=In ‘The Beguiled,’ Pretty Confections Whipped Up to Seduce|work=The New York Times|date=2017-06-30|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2017/06/30/fashion/beguiled-movie-sofia-coppola.html|issn=0362-4331|passage=Not trusting filmgoers to catch the drift, Ms. Coppola underscores the women’s attempts to '''gussy up''' with snippets of arch dialogue.}}
# {{lb|en|informal|transitive}} To make [[fancy]] or [[attractive]], as by [[artificial]] or [[contrived]] means.
#: {{syn|en|spruce up}}
#: {{ux|en|You can have plain green beans, or '''gussie''' them '''up''' with a bit of cheese and onion.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2006|author=Thomas Hackett|title={{w|Slaphappy: Pride, Prejudice, and Professional Wrestling}}|location=New York, NY|publisher=w:HarperCollins|isbn=0-06-019829-X|page=22|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/slaphappypridepr00hack/page/22/mode/2up?q=%22gussied+up%22|passage=WWE and WCW '''gussied up''' the ritual with a lot of shock-and-awe pyrotechnics and the most innovative use of video graphics this side of MTV. Not so Extreme Championship Wrestling.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Jennifer Szalai|title=In ‘Rationality,’ Steven Pinker Sticks Up (Again) for Reason’s Role in Human Progress|work=The New York Times|date=2021-09-29|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/29/books/review-rationality-steven-pinker.html|issn=0362-4331|passage=The trouble arrives when he tries to '''gussy up''' his psychologist’s hat with his more elaborate public intellectual’s attire.}}

